========================================
CSS TRANSITION – INTRODUCTION
========================================

Definition:
-----------
A CSS Transition is used to make a property
change smoothly over a period of time instead
of changing instantly.

It creates a smooth effect between:
1. Initial state
2. Final state


Why We Use Transition:
----------------------
Normally, CSS property changes happen instantly.
Transition makes the change:

• Smooth
• Gradual
• Visually appealing
• Better for user experience


When Transition Works:
-----------------------
Transition works when a property value changes,
such as:

• Hover state (:hover)
• Focus state (:focus)
• Active state (:active)
• When a class is added or removed


What Transition Controls:
--------------------------
1. Which property should animate
2. How long the animation takes
3. The speed pattern of animation
4. When the animation should start


Important Points:
-----------------
• Transition needs a property change.
• Transition needs a duration.
• Without duration, it will NOT work.
• It only works on animatable properties.


Simple Meaning:
---------------
Transition = Smooth change between two states.